    "releaseNotes": "2.5.5 - A second low-tank warning: days of dosing left. New setting \"PushOver low-tank warning at days of dosing left\" (default 14, 0 turns it off) sends one PushOver warning per tank when the tank will run empty in fewer than that many days at the recent daily use. The recent daily use is the chlorine booked over the last 14 days, so a SLAM stretch stops counting 14 days after it ends and a rise in use shows within 14 days. Marking the tank full or correcting the estimate re-arms the warning. The percent warning is unchanged. The tank runway line now shows days until empty beside days until the percent threshold. The warning never blocks or changes a dose. Code update only, no need to press Done.",
